The 1992 Census of Agriculture provides statewide evidence of substantial fertilizer and agricultural chemical use during the period preceding the elevated nitrate measurements identified near Buena Vista–Talbot Roads.

According to Table 15 of the Oregon State Data report, 16,616 farms reported using commercial fertilizer across approximately 2,426,366 acres. Commercial fertilizer expenditures totaled $119.158 million. Agricultural chemical use was reported by 23,952 farms, with expenditures totaling $104.042 million.

Between 1987 and 1992, commercial fertilizer expenditures increased approximately 21.8%, while agricultural chemical expenditures increased approximately 31.2%.

These statistics establish the broader agricultural context in Oregon during the historical nitrate sampling period. They do not establish fertilizer application rates, nitrogen loading, or specific nutrient sources within the Buena Vista–Talbot study area because the figures are statewide aggregates.

Source: 1992 Census of Agriculture, Oregon State Data, Table 15, Agricultural Chemicals Used, Including Fertilizer, printed page 21.
